<link rel="stylesheet" href="static/css/home.css">

<section class="title">
  <h1>Welcome to spood.org!</h1>
</section>

<section>
  <h1>What's this?</h1>
  <p>
    Spood.org is primarily an XMPP chat server run by meeeeeeeeee, spider.
    This is just a landing page for humans, as XMPP clients connect directly to the server backend.
    <br/>
    This domain may sometimes be in use for private projects or testing, and not always available or on this page.
    However, the XMPP server will still be available at spood.org, even if this site is not.
    <br/>
    Unless my certs are out again.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="xmpp">
  <h1>What's XMPP?</h1>
  <div>
    <p>
      XMPP is an open source protocol for a lot of things, but in this case, it's mostly a server for messaging.
      You can access it with any client listed <a href="https://xmpp.org/software"><span class='ul'>here</span></a>, however, spood.org is invite only.
      <br/>
      XMPP is federated, though, so you can sign up elsewhere and message users of spood.org!
      <br/>
      If you'd like to learn more about XMPP, start here: <a href="https://xmpp.org"><span class='ul'>xmpp.org</span></a>
    </p>
    <img src="static/img/xmpp-logo.svg"/>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h1>Can I join, then?</h1>
  <p>
    If you know someone using it and want an account, ask them or email <a href="mailto:admin@spood.org"><span class='ul'>admin@spood.org</span></a>.
    <br/>
    You can always message users of spood.org from another XMPP server-there's a <a href="https://providers.xmpp.net"><span class='ul'>list of free severs here</span></a>,
    and <a href="https://xmpp.org/getting-started"><span class='ul'>steps to get started here</span></a>.
  </p>
</section>
